  "limits": [
    "Engineering fixtures establish mechanisms, not live benefit, live containment or independent human acceptance.",
    "No live Codex or Claude Code journey has run on alpha.44. The beta gate's third run, with both journeys from the start, is what measures these fixes.",
    "The new trusted-local adapter pins, claude-agent-acp 0.101.1 and codex-acp 2.6.0, opened a session under wring job check with Marc's logins and no model prompt, once, on 2026-11-09; no job has run on them. A profile set up earlier keeps 0.65.0 and 1.10.0, and contained images keep their own pins.",
    "The tool list was measured over stdio with a scripted client: 166,286 compact bytes on alpha.43 and 17,542 on this source's binary. A client's token use for it was measured once, for Claude Code after the change only, and is not a before/after comparison.",
    "MCP revisions were measured once per client: Claude Code 2.1.317 initialized at 2025-11-25 after first sending server/discover, which Wringer refuses before initialize; Codex 0.153.4 at 2025-06-18. Nothing was built for server/discover.",
    "Each upgrade check used an archive the tests run built from this commit, not the published asset, on GitHub runners (ubuntu-latest, macos-15). An upgrade on a person's own machine is not measured.",
    "The person sees a job under its first ID; each decision still binds the exact current revision, and a newer revision refuses it. Older jobs show this way too, from the lineage records they already kept.",
    "wring connect adds its project files to .git/info/exclude only when no ignore rule covers them. A file the repository already tracks is edited in place, and the person is told not to commit that change.",
    "A trusted-local delivery is still named contained-… in its records and its evidence commit message, because frozen records name it.",
    "The release run's artifacts were not downloaded; its job records were used."
  ]
